                            <comment id="19698994" author="JIRAUSER129848" created="Thu, 21 May 2026 18:16:28 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=TVanDe17&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;TVanDe17&quot;&gt;Van den broeck, Tamara [JRDBE NON-J&amp;amp;J]&lt;/a&gt; Investigating Ankita&apos;s question about &quot;Edit Layout&quot;, I verified that there is no way to get historical layout information from the API, and so no way to populate this row with any further info. Passing back to Ankita.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="19673370" author="JIRAUSER182813" created="Tue, 19 May 2026 20:17:22 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=CSims11&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;CSims11&quot;&gt;Sims, Cody [JRDUS]&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;b&gt;#Issue 1&lt;/b&gt;-&#160; &lt;font color=&quot;#de350b&quot;&gt;When the Action is Edit Layout, Restore, Trash there are no values in columns Change Type, Details, Old value, New Value. Is that expected?- Cody to investigate&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;#Issue 2&lt;/b&gt;- In audit trail report dates are showing in UTC format in New value/Old value columns, in experiment table it shows as user&apos;s timezone. Is this expected? as discussed post scrum this is expected&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
